## Summary
- Added a community page to showcase DCC members.

## Context
- To add the community page, we had to add 3 react components which are `Community.tsx`, `CommunityCard.tsx` and `Pagination.tsx`.
- If `CommunityCard` component gets null value it renders `CommunityCardSkeleton` component else it renders `CommunityCardComplete`.
- `Pagination` component requires prop drilling for inversion of control. Example:
``` javascript
function ParentComponent = () => {
	//For starting page number
    	const [currentPage, setCurrentPage] = useState(1) 
	//For entries per page. This can be a state variable or a constant depending on use case.
    	const [entryPerPage, setEntryPerPage] =useState(2)
	//Total page count. This can be a state variable or a constant depending on use case.
    	const [totalPage, setTotalPage] = useState(1) 
	//Offset for pagination
    	const offset = 3;

	useEffect(() => {
	
		// todo or fetch function when currentPage or entryPerPage changes.
        
    	}, [currentPage, entryPerPage])

	return (
		<>
			<Pagination paginationProp={{
                    		currentPage: currentPage,
                    		entryPerPage: entryPerPage,
                    		totalPage: totalPage,
                    		offset: offset,
                    		setCurrentPage: setCurrentPage,
                    		setEntryPerPage: setEntryPerPage,
                	}}/>
		</>
	)
}
```
- Also added `useDebounce.tsx` hook for debounce support.
- Added a `useFakeApi.tsx` hook to simulate an API for testing purposes
- Changed the default theme to dark.
